{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Has known your going.</b> He provided for them in everything needed. The expression ״יָדַע״ is like ״וַיֵּדַע אֱלֹהִים״ (Exodus 2:25), ״יְדַעְתִּיךָ בְשֵׁם״ (Exodus 33:12), ״אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ ה׳ פָּנִים אֶל פָּנִים״ (Deuteronomy 34:10), ״מָה אָדָם וַתֵּדָעֵהוּ״ (Psalms 144:3), and many like these. This expression may be said of El, may He be exalted, because all His activity, blessed be He, is through knowledge of Himself." "<b>You have lacked nothing.</b> And they will recognize that you took nothing from them for your own needs, but you benefited them out of brotherhood, and so that they would come to you and see the deeds of HaShem and His wonders."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:13.137672125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}